# Text files are LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, a contributor's tooling decides: a Python script that writes a tracked
# file with the platform default newline turns `file.md` into CRLF on Windows and LF on
# Linux, and the diff - 600 to 2,500 lines for a content change of a dozen - passes every
# test, because nothing reads line endings. Two hooks now enforce what this declares.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fuzz corpora and crash payloads are raw byte streams; the bytes ARE the
# input, so text normalization (CRLF handling) must never touch them. The
# committed seeds join the two ephemeral dirs: several carry a bare CR or a
# trailing space as part of the reproduction (`&"X-\r:`, `!y5%7c `), which a
# contributor with core.autocrlf enabled would otherwise silently rewrite.
fuzz/corpus/** -text
fuzz/artifacts/** -text
fuzz/seeds/** -text

# Binary: never diff or normalize.
*.pyd binary
*.so binary
*.pyd-* binary
*.dll binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
